{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527005-question-about-resisting-presence-v20-and-vda20-and-the-revelations-of-eden-vda20","id":1527005,"title":"Question about resisting Presence (V20 and VDA20) and the Revelations of Eden (VDA20)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-17T15:27:37-08:00","id":1527005,"title":"Question about resisting Presence (V20 and VDA20) and the Revelations of Eden (VDA20)","content":"Hello there,<br /> <br /> The text for resisting Presence: &quot;Anyone can resist Presence for one scene by spending a Willpower point and succeeding on a Willpower roll (difficulty 8)&quot;<br /> The text for resisting Revelations of Eden: &quot;The victim may attempt to resist the effects of the Discipline with a Willpower roll (difficulty 6).&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm reading both, but especially the second, as referring to a <i>resisted</i><i> roll</i>, meaning that each success by the victim reduces the Presence- or Revelations of Eden-user's successes by 1, <b>NOT </b>that 1 success is enough to cancel (temporarily, in the case of Presence) the power even if the user rolled several successes. Am I wrong? Is there conclusive proof? I see the word &quot;resist&quot; used, which is a technical term in the game system, and also both powers would be pretty useless if anyone with Willpower 3+ (what's needed to average 1 success on diff.6) or 5+ (to average 1 success on diff.8) could dismiss them more often than not.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-03T19:57:58-07:00","id":1538068,"title":"","content":"A <i>resisted roll</i> is a type of roll. <i>To resist </i>a power is a type of outcome. Similar words, but completely different categories of rules.<br /> <br /> The <i>powers</i> are resisted, but the <i>roll</i> to do so is a simple one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T06:39:52-07:00","id":1538129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527005-question-about-resisting-presence-v20-and-vda20-and-the-revelations-of-eden-vda20?p=1538068#post1538068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A <i>resisted roll</i> is a type of roll. <i>To resist </i>a power is a type of outcome. Similar words, but completely different categories of rules.<br /> <br /> The <i>powers</i> are resisted, but the <i>roll</i> to do so is a simple one.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you are saying that one success by the victim is sufficient to deny the power regardless of the successes rolled by the user?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T15:38:28-07:00","id":1538155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527005-question-about-resisting-presence-v20-and-vda20-and-the-revelations-of-eden-vda20?p=1538129#post1538129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you are saying that one success by the victim is sufficient to deny the power regardless of the successes rolled by the user?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, precisely.<br /> <br /> That's one of the important distinctions between Presence and Dominate: Presence is an easier power to resist.<br /> <br /> Or what is maybe a better interpretation, its effect is to drain Willpower <i>en masse</i>, but letting the victims choose to succumb to uncontrolled emotion if they want to preserve that Willpower.<br /> <br /> Not going too much on a tangent here, bottom line is yes, you can resist with a single success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-05T18:37:50-07:00","id":1538161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527005-question-about-resisting-presence-v20-and-vda20-and-the-revelations-of-eden-vda20?p=1538155#post1538155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, precisely.<br /> <br /> That's one of the important distinctions between Presence and Dominate: Presence is an easier power to resist.<br /> <br /> Or what is maybe a better interpretation, its effect is to drain Willpower <i>en masse</i>, but letting the victims choose to succumb to uncontrolled emotion if they want to preserve that Willpower.<br /> <br /> Not going too much on a tangent here, bottom line is yes, you can resist with a single success.</div> </div> </div> </div>i understand your point. It seems reasonable and what's most important, is that it works at your table.<br /> <br /> Personally, I've come to the conclusion that, if I am the ST, I would run those powers the other way, as resisted rolls, though the victim. it seems fairer to me and more balanced.<br /> <br /> In VDA20 there is no resistance to Dominate: no roll, except to avoid making eye contact, and even that presupposes one knows eye contact would be a risk, and I think it's mainly to prevent players (and STs) to simply declare they don't look into the other person's eyes and permanently avoid Dominate. Instead of letting them dec\u0323lare where they look, they roll. Therefore, the fact that Presence affords resistance at all is already enough difference.<br /> <br /> As for Presence working en masse, that is only true of Awe and Majesty. Majesty is a 5 dots power and already has its own rules on how spending Willpower and rolling allows victims to resist. Awe is a 1 dot power on difficulty 7. 1 success affects 1 person; 2, 2 people; 3, 6 people; 4, 20 people; 5, all those in the vampire's immediate vicinity. Assuming a vampire has 10 dots between Charisma and Performance (the maximum for most pcs, raised to 12 if they're 7th gen), and that he has a relevant specialisation (which my ST does not apply to Disciplines, but I would), he would average 4 successes. 3 without specialisation. 6 or 20 people are going to be affected, picked from those with the lowest Willpower nearby. The vampire will be able to add his Presence rating to social rolls against them based on the particular impression he chose to give when he activated the power. And then social rolls are heavily up to ST's interpretation for resolution, and don't produce excessive change in people unless there are other grounds for it. I don't find this power to be well described as draining Willpower en masse, even if it has some potential to. Statistically it doesn't pack enough of a punch.<br /> <br /> As for Dread Gaze, Entrancement and Summon, they don't work en masse, but it makes sense to attempt to resist them through Willpower expenditure. Still, if all it takes is Willpower 5 to resist them on average, I don't see how they would ever work effectively for anyone. Dread Gaze is typically needed in the moment, so by the time one has spent 1 Willpower point and passed the roll with one success, becoming immune for the scene, much of its usefulness is gone. With Entrancement and Summon, they're still somewhat useful even if the victim resists initially, but then, they are level 3 and 4 powers, so I would hope they actually get to do something.<br /> <br /> This is my reasoning in detail. But as I said, I find yours reasonable, even though it does not convince me.<br /> <br /> As for Revelations of Eden, since it has no duration, it would be completely useless statistically against anyone with Willpower 3+, and it would not even cost the victim 1 Willpower point to resist. Realistically, the Setites of Constantinople would not have had much reason to strive to learn it from the Witches if it worked so rarely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 07-05-2024, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-06T10:02:04-07:00","id":1538173,"title":"","content":"I won't go in detail because I don't have the time right now. Suffice to say, Presence at least is meant for use in distinct contexts and against distinct victims, among other things not being much geared towards affecting other Vampires, but being very good at manipulating mortals.<br /> <br /> Either way, this reasoning is to explain the logic behind RAW. Enough tables don't use Presence as it was designed to work, and if making the roll resisted works at your table, so be it.<br /> <br /> But RAW, it only requires 1 success, and that is by design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}